# --- W2-TAG words ---
# M-TAG — shape polymorphism.  Since M-TAG2 (W9-2A) a GOLF value is a LIST iff
# its top 16 bits are exactly 0x7FFF (W11-1A; 0x0001 before) — a heap address
# tagged with 0x7FFF<<48, which is
# what every list word returns; everything else is an INT, including the -1/0
# flags \eq/\rlt produce (top bits 0xFFFF), every negative number and every
# value below 0x7FFF<<48 — in particular a raw heap address.  The integers
# sacrificed are [0x7FFF<<48, 2^63), the 2^48 just below INT64_MAX.  Until M-TAG2
# this was a RANGE test against the heap-bounds cells, which classified an integer that happened to equal a heap address as a
# list; the cells are now A's alone.
# Top-level init: the prelude is prepended source, so plain tokens run at program
# start, before any user code.  W6/M-MEM moved that init to the "W6 allocator"
# block below, where it asks the kernel for the bounds instead of naming them —
# both cells are still written before anything can allocate or call T, because
# every allocation happens in a word body and user code runs last.
# T  v -> 0 (list) / 1 (int).  Zero-is-true, so `T[…]` runs the LIST path.
# v>>48 (logical) is 32767 exactly for a tagged list (a negative gives 65535); \eq makes that -1/0 and 1\radd
# maps it to 0/1.  A leaf: no scratch, hence no spill frame, hence callable anywhere
# — including from inside D's own dispatch, where scratch is live.
:T48>32767\eq1\radd;
# K  list s fn -> list   new[i] = fn(list[i], s)      broadcast list ⊙ scalar
# G  s list fn -> list   new[i] = fn(s, list[i])      broadcast scalar ⊙ list
# Two words rather than one plus an argument swap, because fn need not commute —
# ∸ and its order are exactly the point.  Structure is M's: X/Y frame, s0 list,
# s1 index, s3 fn, s4 result, s7 the parked scalar; the length header is written
# outside the `0\eq[…]` guard so the empty list yields an empty list; every
# pointer/index/flag step is a raw op.  fn sees user data and so stays \exec'd.
# W4A: s7 is a 64-bit cell now, so the parked scalar keeps its full width — the
# old wart where `-3 ⍳4 +` broadcast 4294967293 (a 32-bit round trip through
# scratch) is GONE, and a negative or >= 2^32 broadcast scalar survives intact.
:K X5177464\store5177496\store16\shl16>5177440\store5177440\fetch\fetch"1\radd A"5177472\store\store0 5177448\store5177440\fetch\fetch0\eq[{5177440\fetch5177448\fetch I5177496\fetch5177464\fetch\exec5177472\fetch5177448\fetch8\rmul\radd8\radd\store5177448\fetch1\radd5177448\store5177448\fetch5177440\fetch\fetch\rlt1\radd}]5177472\fetch32767 48\shl| Y;
:G X5177464\store16\shl16>5177440\store5177496\store5177440\fetch\fetch"1\radd A"5177472\store\store0 5177448\store5177440\fetch\fetch0\eq[{5177496\fetch5177440\fetch5177448\fetch I5177464\fetch\exec5177472\fetch5177448\fetch8\rmul\radd8\radd\store5177448\fetch1\radd5177448\store5177448\fetch5177440\fetch\fetch\rlt1\radd}]5177472\fetch32767 48\shl| Y;
# D  a b fn -> c   the binary shape dispatcher, and the calling convention M-VEC
# will route the bare + - * ⌈ ⌊ templates through: fn is a quotation address.
# a and b are NEVER parked in scratch — they stay on the data stack, so the
# int,int path hands fn its operands at full 64-bit width and the list paths hand
# Z/K/G the very words they want.  `&` reaches under the flag being built, so the
# only state is s3 (fn) and s2 (the shape code 2*T(a)+T(b): 0 ll · 1 li · 2 il ·
# 3 ii), both covered by X/Y.  Guards are `code k\rsub[…]` — zero, so true, only
# for its own k — and exactly one fires; Z/K/G restore s2 as they leave, so the
# guards after the one that ran still read the code and not someone's garbage.
:D X5177464\store&T2\rmul&T\radd5177456\store5177456\fetch[5177464\fetch Z]5177456\fetch1\rsub[5177464\fetch K]5177456\fetch2\rsub[5177464\fetch G]5177456\fetch3\rsub[5177464\fetch\exec]Y;
# The user-facing polymorphic operators, bytes 0xC0..0xC4 (REGISTRY.md §1.2).
# Until W9-3B ∔ ∸ ⨰ were three tokens each — ′atom auto-wrapped the raw scalar
# op in a thunk and D picked the shape, ONE level deep.  The definition name is the high byte itself — `:\vadd` is `: 0xC0`.
# W9-3B: DEEP.  Each hands D the word ITSELF, as ⩌ ⩍ below always did, so Z/K/G
# re-enter it per element and an element that is a list dispatches again — to
# any depth (`2⍳′⍳€ 10+` adds 10 at every level).  That rules out D's int,int
# path (it would ⍎ the word on two ints and loop), so int,int is answered in
# place with the raw op and ^.  The bare + - * still reach here only through the
# template's tag filter, so the scalar fast path never sees this word.
